      "Deposit-protecting move-out steps for WeHo's dense rental market.",
    contentHtml: `
<p>West Hollywood is one of the densest, most renter-heavy cities in Los Angeles County, with a housing stock dominated by mid-century apartment buildings, rent-stabilized units, and a tenant base that turns over frequently. That density means property managers and landlords in WeHo tend to have well-practiced move-out inspection routines, and they compare each unit against a fairly consistent standard: clean, undamaged, and ready for the next tenant. For renters, that translates into real money on the line. A thorough move-out cleaning is one of the most reliable ways to protect your security deposit, and in a market where units turn over quickly, landlords rarely have patience for a lengthy back-and-forth over cleaning charges.</p>
<p>This guide walks through what to clean, when to clean it, and how to document your work so you leave your WeHo apartment on good terms — and with your deposit intact.</p>

<h2>Move-Out Cleaning Checklist</h2>
<p>Most landlord walkthroughs focus on a handful of high-traffic areas. If you only have time to clean a few rooms thoroughly, prioritize these.</p>

<h3>Kitchen</h3>
<p>The kitchen is usually the first place a landlord checks, since grease and food residue build up quickly and are easy to spot. Wipe down the inside and outside of the refrigerator, including the door seals and any drawers, and unplug and defrost the freezer if needed. Clean the oven interior, stovetop, and range hood filter, since baked-on grease is one of the most common deposit deductions. Wipe out cabinets and drawers, clean the sink and faucet, and don't forget the tops of cabinets and the space behind and under the refrigerator, where dust and grime tend to collect unnoticed.</p>

<h3>Bathroom</h3>
<p>Bathrooms are inspected closely for soap scum, mildew, and mineral buildup. Scrub the tub or shower, including grout lines and any glass doors, and clean the toilet inside and out, including the base and hinges. Wipe down the mirror, sink, and countertop, and clean inside the medicine cabinet and vanity drawers. Check the exhaust fan cover for dust, since it's a spot many renters overlook but landlords often check.</p>

<h3>Closets and Storage</h3>
<p>Empty closets completely and vacuum or sweep the floor, including corners where dust and debris accumulate. Wipe down shelving and any built-in drawers, and check closet tracks and door runners, which can trap dirt over time. If your unit has extra storage such as a hallway linen closet or a balcony storage box, give those the same treatment — landlords in older WeHo buildings often inspect these spaces during a walkthrough since they're easy to forget.</p>

<h3>Floors</h3>
<p>Floors should be the last thing you clean, since they'll show footprints from everything else you do. Vacuum carpets thoroughly, paying attention to corners and under furniture footprints, and consider a deeper carpet clean if there are visible stains. For hard flooring, sweep first, then mop, making sure to get baseboards and corners where dust collects. Pay special attention to entryways and areas near the kitchen and bathroom, which tend to accumulate the most buildup over a lease term.</p>

<h2>Timing Your Clean Around the Move and Walkthrough</h2>
<p>Cleaning too early can mean redoing work after the movers track dust and debris back through the unit. Cleaning too late can mean rushing through a checklist right as your landlord is knocking on the door. The most reliable approach is to schedule your deep clean after all furniture and boxes are out of the unit, but before your scheduled walkthrough.</p>
<p>In a building-dense area like West Hollywood, move dates often bump up against tight elevator reservation windows or loading dock schedules, so it helps to plan cleaning as its own separate block of time rather than squeezing it in around the movers. If your building requires a specific move-out date and a separate inspection appointment, treat the cleaning as the step that happens in between — once the space is empty, but before the landlord or property manager walks through with you.</p>
<p>Because move-out day can be unpredictable, especially in walk-up buildings or units with limited parking for moving trucks, many renters choose to book a professional move-out cleaning to fall on a fixed schedule rather than trying to fit it in personally at the last minute. This is especially useful if your lease end date and your move date aren't the same day, since it gives you a buffer to handle the clean without racing the clock.</p>

<h2>Documenting the Finished Condition</h2>
<p>Once the unit is clean, take time-stamped photos or a short video walkthrough of every room, including closets, appliances, and any areas that had previous damage or wear noted on your move-in checklist. This documentation is your best protection if a landlord later disputes the condition of the unit or the return of your deposit.</p>
<p>California caps most residential security deposits at one month's rent, which makes the deposit itself a meaningful amount to protect. Keep your photos organized by room and date them clearly, and if your landlord conducts a walkthrough with you in person, ask for any notes or concerns in writing at the time rather than after the fact. If you used a professional cleaning service, keep the receipt or confirmation as an additional record that the unit was cleaned to a professional standard before you handed back the keys.</p>

<h2>Leaving on Good Terms</h2>
<p>Move-out cleaning in a market as fast-moving as West Hollywood doesn't have to be stressful. A room-by-room checklist, a clean handoff between move-out and walkthrough, and clear documentation go a long way toward protecting your deposit and leaving a good impression with your landlord or property manager. For renters short on time during a move, Spottly's <a href="/services/move-in-move-out-cleaning">move-in move-out cleaning service</a> and local <a href="/service-areas/west-hollywood">West Hollywood cleaning services</a> are built around exactly this kind of deadline-driven clean.</p>

<p>Moving out of a WeHo apartment? <a href="/contact">Request a free move-out cleaning quote from Spottly</a>.</p>
`,
